{
	"name": "Fungal Drake",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/creatures/abilities/dragon-breath-purple.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Though they may resemble dragons made miniature, fungal drakes lack a breath weapon, cannot speak, and are seldom larger than the average house cat. They sport a variety of brightly-colored fungal growths protruding from their bodies that can resemble mushrooms, lichens, and other fungi found both above and below ground. A tamed fungal drake is often a part of a noble’s menagerie for their talent of discerning which mushrooms are safe to eat. When startled, they emit a small cloud of mildly irritating spores before they try to flee. Adventurers who are within a 10-foot radius of a frightened fungal drake must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution saving throw or be incapacitated by a coughing fit for 1 minute.</p><p>Fungal drakes have a fast metabolism and a highly specialized diet comprised of mushrooms that are incredibly difficult to source on the road. Adventurers who wish to keep a tamed fungal drake as a pet must spend 5 gp per day to keep their pet fed. If a fungal drake goes more than 3 days without food, it starves.</p>",
